From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] pair standard WMI RX promiscuous filter in short slots

The pinned firmware API explicitly defines a separate fixed-parameter
WMI_PDEV_SET_RX_FILTER_PROMISCUOUS_CMDID with pdev_id and enable/disable
field, plus a TLV validation table. Use that declared command, not guessed
WMI_PDEV_PARAM_RX_FILTER bit masks or old-generation parameter numbers.
A new root load-time flag defaults off. When enabled, each existing bounded
slot queues enable before channel/capture work and always queues disable
before normal RX restoration, even on failure. Convert host pdev IDs using
the existing WMI mapping. Existing vdev operation guard, dwell/frequency bounds,
channel/home restore and independent stock rollback remain.
Host queue success does not prove firmware acceptance; capture and measure it.
No firmware blob or persistent driver replacement is performed.

